WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.704
(upbeat jazzy music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:01.704 --> 00:00:03.529
- Alright, let's share
one more great story

00:00:03.529 --> 00:00:04.653
before we have to say goodbye.

00:00:04.653 --> 00:00:05.917
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:05.917 --> 00:00:09.011
(upbeat jazzy music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:09.011 --> 00:00:11.330
Practically every school library has them.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:13.890
I'm talking about the "Ordinary
People Change the World"

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.990
book series from author Brad Meltzer

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.300
and illustrator Chris Eliopoulos.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.900
The series covers icons from
Abraham Lincoln to Rosa Parks

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.970
and has sold over 7 million copies.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.400
Their latest is "I am Ruth Bader Ginsburg"

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.830
profiling the late Supreme Court justice.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:29.760
It's out now

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.460
and it marks the 10th
anniversary of the series.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.540
So on the line right now

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.610
to talk about it is author Brad Meltzer.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:36.530
Give it up for him, y'all!

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:37.779
(audience clapping)

00:00:37.779 --> 00:00:40.252
Welcome back to the show, Brad!

00:00:40.252 --> 00:00:42.613
- Good to see you. So good to be back.

00:00:42.613 --> 00:00:45.270
- So these books we've talked
about, they're so successful.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.683
How does this feel, man?

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.010
- It feels like my family
bought a lot of copies,

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:50.892
is what it feels like.

00:00:50.892 --> 00:00:52.470
(audience laughs)
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.600
The truth is, is it's humbling.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.100
We started this series as you know,

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.440
to give our kids better
heroes to look up to,

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.800
and it's amazing to watch
now 7 million parents

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:02.940
and kids reading the books.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:06.120
We're going on a
nationwide tour, 12 cities.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.640
Lynda Carter, who played Wonder
Woman, is gonna be with us

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:09.473
in Virginia.

00:01:09.473 --> 00:01:11.550
Temple Grandin is gonna be with us

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:12.383
in Colorado.
(audience clapping)

00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:13.216
We're going to Atlanta

00:01:13.216 --> 00:01:14.160
and Texas and Florida
- [Kelly] So cool!

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.380
- and everywhere in
between, meeting parents

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:20.070
and kids who are determined to
make the world a better place

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.360
with a bit more decency in it

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.730
because man, that's what we
need right now. Right, Kelly?

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:24.900
- Absolutely.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.480
Well the the latest book
"I am Ruth Bader Ginsburg,"

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:28.740
you actually knew her, right?

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:29.573
- I did.

00:01:29.573 --> 00:01:31.230
It's the only hero we've done who I knew

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.330
before we did a book on her

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:34.260
and I know her

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.530
because her daughter was
actually one of my mentors

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.970
when I was in school.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.700
And the other thing that's
crazy is one of her clerks,

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.350
when she was a Supreme Court justice,

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.970
was one of my best friends.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.710
So at my friend's wedding,
- [Kelly] Huh.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.230
- her witnesses for the
marriage certificate,

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.430
to sign the marriage certificate,

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.770
were myself and Justice Ginsburg.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.240
And so we're sitting in the room

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.370
and she signs the marriage certificate

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:58.890
and there goes Justice
Ginsburg, signs her name

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.180
and I look at my friend and I'm like,

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:01.942
do you really need me at this point?

00:02:01.942 --> 00:02:03.030
(audience laughing)
- (laughing) Do you really,

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.910
Do you really want my
signature? (laughing)

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.380
That's amazing!

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:10.620
Alright, so what do you want
kids to take away from this?

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.420
- You know, I think that when we think

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.500
of Ruth Bader Ginsburg,

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.680
we think of this like stately
Supreme Court justice,

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.960
but we forget when she was just a girl,

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.940
Ruth Bader Ginsburg liked
going roller skating.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.210
She liked climbing trees
and having adventures.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.920
But this was something back then

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.600
that girls weren't supposed to do.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.070
It was boys who had the adventures.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:31.110
It was even the books she used to read.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:34.050
Boys would go climbing trees
and jumping all over the place

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.450
and the girls would
wear pretty pink dresses

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.834
and sit there and watch.

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:38.667
- Mhm.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.950
- And it was her mother
who broke that stereotype.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.080
Her mom, when she was a
little girl, used to take her

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.100
to the library

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:47.220
and every Friday said, "you
could pick out five books."

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.160
And her favorite books were
the books about real heroes.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.530
Amelia Earhart, Harriet Tubman.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.660
And it was those heroes, like her mother,

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.400
who taught her that same lesson.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.730
There is absolutely nothing
that a girl can't do.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.320
And I want my daughter
to have that lesson.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.153
(audience clapping)
I want my sons

00:03:02.153 --> 00:03:03.360
to have that lesson.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.670
I want everyone and, and
here's the finale of the book.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:07.932
It says, "Today they
call me a trailblazer.

00:03:07.932 --> 00:03:11.730
But the best part of blazing
a trail is leaving tracks.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.770
That means you're not just
doing things for yourself,

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:16.200
you're leaving a path
for others to follow.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.153
Start with one voice and
let it grow into a chorus.

00:03:19.153 --> 00:03:22.822
I am Ruth Bader Ginsburg. Create
equality. Create justice."

00:03:22.822 --> 00:03:24.762
(audience clapping)
- Absolutely.

00:03:24.762 --> 00:03:26.217
Thank you so much, Brad.

00:03:26.217 --> 00:03:28.537
We love having you on the
show. Love this new book.

00:03:28.537 --> 00:03:30.630
"I am Ruth Bader Ginsburg" is out now

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:32.386
and everyone is going home with a copy!

00:03:32.386 --> 00:03:34.427
(audience cheering)
(audience clapping)

00:03:34.427 --> 00:03:36.578
- For more information on
where you can meet Brad

00:03:36.578 --> 00:03:40.062
and illustrator Chris
Eliopoulos, head to our socials.

00:03:40.062 --> 00:03:41.027
Thank you so much, Brad. I'm
liking your post right now.

00:03:43.614 --> 00:03:44.447
That's not all.

00:03:44.447 --> 00:03:47.795
Our season-long partner
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:03:47.795 --> 00:03:49.043
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:03:49.043 --> 00:03:51.270
want to celebrate your book series

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.220
and the life of Justice Ginsburg.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.140
So what they're gonna do is
they're gonna write a check

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:56.430
for a thousand dollars

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:59.158
to the Women's Suffrage
National Monument Foundation.

00:03:59.158 --> 00:04:00.851
(audience cheering)

00:04:00.851 --> 00:04:02.340
We know you're a big supporter,

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.820
so trying to get that built
in Washington DC right now.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:07.310
Thank you so much Brad,

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:08.762
and thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:04:08.762 --> 00:04:12.095
Jon Cryer, Joe Keery, Danielle Carters,

00:04:12.095 --> 00:04:14.830
(drowned out)

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:15.854
It's not changing.

